      "refersTo": "icon-button",
      "description": "40px square ghost button for menu, close and theme toggle.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-icon-btn\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Open navigation\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"12\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"6\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"18\" y2=\"18\"/></svg></button>",
      "css": ":host{--surface-0:#0e1013;--surface-1:#08090b;--surface-2:#16191e;--surface-3:#1f232a;--line:#262a31;--line-strong:#353a43;--ink:#f2f4f7;--ink-2:#a9b0bb;--ink-3:#8a919c;--accent:#e10600;--accent-ink:#ff4136;--on-accent:#fff;--best:#b98bff;--gain:#3ddc84;--caution:#ffc21a;--danger:#ff4136;--shadow:0 1px 2px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4),0 8px 24px -8px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);} .ds-icon-btn{display:grid;place-items:center;width:40px;height:40px;border:0;border-radius:6px;background:transparent;color:var(--ink-2);cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 150ms,color 150ms;} .ds-icon-btn:hover{background:var(--surface-3);color:var(--ink);} .ds-icon-btn:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent-ink,#ff4136);outline-offset:2px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Season Select",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "select",
      "description": "Native select with inline uppercase label.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-field\"><span>Season</span><select class=\"ds-select\"><option>Current (2026)</option><option>2025</option></select></label>",
      "css": ":host{--surface-0:#0e1013;--surface-1:#08090b;--surface-2:#16191e;--surface-3:#1f232a;--line:#262a31;--line-strong:#353a43;--ink:#f2f4f7;--ink-2:#a9b0bb;--ink-3:#8a919c;--accent:#e10600;--accent-ink:#ff4136;--on-accent:#fff;--best:#b98bff;--gain:#3ddc84;--caution:#ffc21a;--danger:#ff4136;--shadow:0 1px 2px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4),0 8px 24px -8px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);} .ds-field{font-family:'Archivo',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;} .ds-field span{font-size:0.6875rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3,#8a919c);} .ds-select{font:inherit;height:40px;padding:0 32px 0 12px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:6px;background:var(--surface-2);color:var(--ink);font-size:0.875rem;font-weight:500;cursor:pointer;} .ds-select:hover{border-color:var(--ink-3);} .ds-select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent-ink,#ff4136);outline-offset:2px;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Timing Tower",
    "overview": "The dashboard reads like a broadcast timing tower. Positions, points and gaps are the loudest marks on screen, set in condensed bold numerals with tabular figures so columns never jitter. Team color is identity and lives only in a narrow vertical stripe beside the team name; the chrome around it stays neutral carbon (dark) or cool paper-grey (light).\n\nDensity is moderate and list-led: content is a stack of hairline-bordered panels on a faint dot grid, and the primary data shape is a row (position, stripe, name, points, gap), not a card per item. F1 red is spent sparingly on the active nav block, focus, selection and the wordmark. Timing-sector semantics carry state: purple for best/leader, green for gain, amber for caution.\n\nThe system rejects the generic dark SaaS dashboard of same-size glowing cards and the neon-on-black \"racing\" costume. Dark is the default experience; light is a full peer theme, not an inversion afterthought.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Condensed (wdth 68) bold Archivo for numerals and headings; normal-width Archivo for UI.",
      "Tabular figures on everything (set on `body`).",
      "Two-layer neutrals: rail and top bar sit a step darker than the content area in both themes.",
      "Hairline borders, one 6px radius, one soft raised shadow.",
      "Team color appears only as a 4px stripe, always paired with the team name."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Neutral Chrome Rule",
        "body": "The UI shell never takes a team color or a decorative hue. Red marks the active place and focus; everything else is ink on carbon.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Fill, Red Ink Rule",
        "body": "`accent` is a fill; `accent-ink` is the text/line red. Do not swap them.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sector Semantics Rule",
        "body": "Purple, green and amber mean best, gain and caution, as on a timing screen. Never use them decoratively.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Everything Rule",
        "body": "Tabular figures are on globally; every numeric column right-aligns so digits stack.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Label Is Not A Kicker Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase labels name a column, a stat or a control. They never sit above a heading as an eyebrow.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Chrome Rule",
        "body": "Rail, top bar and controls carry no shadow; separation comes from surface tone and a hairline.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set positions, points, stats and headings in condensed bold Archivo (font-stretch 68%, weight 700) and keep tabular figures on.",
      "Do show team identity with the 4px team stripe next to the team name, never by color alone.",
      "Do use `accent` (#E10600) only as a fill with white text, and `accent-ink` whenever red is text or an outline.",
      "Do use `best` purple for leader/fastest, `gain` green for improvement and `caution` amber for warnings.",
      "Do build lists as timing-tower rows with hairline dividers, right-aligned numeric columns and a label-caps column head.",
      "Do keep targets at 40px, give every view loading, empty and error states, and gate motion behind reduced-motion checks.",
      "Do define every new color in both `[data-theme=\"dark\"]` and `[data-theme=\"light\"]` and map it through `@theme inline`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't put team colors on chrome, card fills, headings or large areas; they belong to the stripe.",
      "Don't set text in `accent` (#E10600) on dark surfaces; it fails 4.5:1.",
      "Don't use purple, green or amber decoratively.",
      "Don't place an uppercase label above a heading as an eyebrow.",
      "Don't add glow, neon, gradients or hard offset shadows; the only shadow is Raised, on panels.",
      "Don't introduce a second radius or a second typeface."
    ]
  }
}
